{"_id":"6ac76e8b54ecd7719cf2171e","id":"Emulated-Inc/sci-spinal-cord-structure-injury","author":"Emulated-Inc","sha":"88d2f1c2ad52b004762a381f574df2712b971d01","lastModified":"2026-10-08T10:21:27.000Z","private":false,"gated":false,"disabled":false,"tags":["license:cc-by-4.0","region:us"],"description":"\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tSpineDL structure sections (training animals)\n\t\n\ntrain.tar holds 56 confocal sections of thoracic mouse spinal cord (DAPI and NeuN, two-channel 8-bit TIFF) from\n18 animals, each with its structure map (0 outside the section, 1 grey matter, 2 central canal, 3 white matter,\n4 damaged tissue), and sections.csv with each section's animal (anonymised) and pixel size in micrometres.\nImages and maps are byte-identical copies of files in the SpineDL dataset, renamed.\nSource: Ruiz-Amezcua… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Emulated-Inc/sci-spinal-cord-structure-injury.","downloads":41,"likes":0,"cardData":{"license":"cc-by-4.0","pretty_name":"SpineDL structure sections, training animals"},"siblings":[{"rfilename":".gitattributes"},{"rfilename":"README.md"},{"rfilename":"train.tar"}],"createdAt":"2026-10-08T10:20:59.000Z","usedStorage":1127372800}